doc:sch-1-sec-56ao-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "56AO(2) Extraterritorial operation of the CDR provisions" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) To the extent that the CDR provisions have effect in relation to CDR data held within Australia, the CDR provisions apply in relation to all persons (including foreign persons). CDR provisions can apply for CDR data held outside Australia" ;
    cof:pageNumber "18"^^xsd:integer .

concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ao-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56AO(3) Extraterritorial operation of the CDR provisions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56ao-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) To the extent that the CDR provisions have effect in relation to an act, or omission, relating to CDR data held outside Australia, the CDR provisions only apply if:  (a) the act or omission is by (or on behalf of) an Australian person; or  Consumer data right  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 63, 2019 Treasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019  (b) the act or omission occurs wholly or partly in Australia, or wholly or partly on board an Australian aircraft or an Australian ship; or  (c) the act or omission occurs wholly outside Australia, and an Australian person suffers, or is likely to suffer, financial or other disadvantage as a result of the act or omission. Interpretation" ;
    skos:definition "(3) To the extent that the CDR provisions have effect in relation to an act, or omission, relating to CDR data held outside Australia, the CDR provisions only apply if:  (a) the act or omission is by (or on behalf of) an Australian person; or  Consumer data right  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 63, 2019 Treasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019  (b) the act or omission occurs wholly or partly in Australia, or wholly or partly on board an Australian aircraft or an Australian ship; or  (c) the act or omission occurs wholly outside Australia, and an Australian person suffers, or is likely to suffer, financial or other disadvantage as a result of the act or omission. Interpretation"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "47b84888c48928b54d832c03f6fba27e28c24361c9f50b8556422415c0e8e1e0" ;
    values:partOf concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ao ;
    cof:pageNumber "18"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "CDR provisions apply to acts or omissions outside Australia if they affect an Australian person." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
