concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56aq a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56AQ CDR provisions bind the Crown"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56aq ;
    values:originalText "(1) The CDR provisions bind the Crown in each of its capacities.  (2) However, the CDR provisions do not make the Crown:  (a) liable to a pecuniary penalty or to be prosecuted for an offence; or  (b) subject to a remedy under section 56EY (about actions for damages for contravening the privacy safeguards); or  (c) subject to a remedy under Part VI (about enforcement) other than section 87B (about enforceable undertakings); or  (d) subject to a remedy under Part 4 (about civil penalties) or 7 (about injunctions) of the Regulatory Powers Act; or  (e) subject to Part XID of this Act (about search and seizure)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The CDR provisions bind the Crown in each of its capacities.  (2) However, the CDR provisions do not make the Crown:  (a) liable to a pecuniary penalty or to be prosecuted for an offence; or  (b) subject to a remedy under section 56EY (about actions for damages for contravening the privacy safeguards); or  (c) subject to a remedy under Part VI (about enforcement) other than section 87B (about enforceable undertakings); or  (d) subject to a remedy under Part 4 (about civil penalties) or 7 (about injunctions) of the Regulatory Powers Act; or  (e) subject to Part XID of this Act (about search and seizure)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8837e13dea7d6c8567c001676d6cd3f3f53171aed4cfe4c97770c17aed201cb9" ;
