concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bh-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56BH(3) Rules about accreditation of data recipients"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56bh-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) Without limiting paragraph (1)(e), each of the following may be a ground for varying, suspending or revoking an accreditation:  (a) a failure to comply with a requirement in this Part or in the consumer data rules;  (b) a failure to comply with a requirement in the privacy safeguards. Note: An example of a variation could be the imposition of a condition, or changing the level of an accreditation." ;
    skos:definition "(3) Without limiting paragraph (1)(e), each of the following may be a ground for varying, suspending or revoking an accreditation:  (a) a failure to comply with a requirement in this Part or in the consumer data rules;  (b) a failure to comply with a requirement in the privacy safeguards. Note: An example of a variation could be the imposition of a condition, or changing the level of an accreditation."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "df6ca88c124ad3ecd57cf6364cd86b4f63b5d95f34228cf39795fc66d1f28512" ;
    values:partOf concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bh ;
    cof:pageNumber "30"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Failure to comply with requirements may result in varying, suspending or revoking accreditation." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf> ;
