concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bh-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56BH(4) Rules about accreditation of data recipients"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56bh-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) If the consumer data rules include rules enabling decisions to be made to vary, suspend or revoke accreditations, the rules must permit the making of applications to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for review of those decisions. Note: The consumer data rules can also provide for internal review of these decisions, and internal and AAT review of other decisions (see section 56BJ)." ;
    skos:definition "(4) If the consumer data rules include rules enabling decisions to be made to vary, suspend or revoke accreditations, the rules must permit the making of applications to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for review of those decisions. Note: The consumer data rules can also provide for internal review of these decisions, and internal and AAT review of other decisions (see section 56BJ)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4f7e664093a361179ce18b8ef1567ed2175527515eff35a81127ddde84ee5a7d" ;
    values:partOf concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bh ;
    cof:pageNumber "30"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Must permit applications to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for review of decisions." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
