concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bo a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56BO Misleading or deceptive conduct—civil penalty"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56bo ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person must not engage in conduct that misleads or deceives, or is likely to mislead or deceive, another person (the second person) into believing that:  (a) a person is a CDR consumer for CDR data; or  (b) a person is making a valid request or consent, or has satisfied other criteria, for the disclosure of CDR data under the consumer data rules. Note 1: The person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) could be the first-mentioned person, the second person or a third person. Note 2: For enforcement, see Part VI (including section 76 for an order for payment of a pecuniary penalty). Defence  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the conduct is not misleading or deceptive in a material particular.  (3) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (2) bears the burden of adducing or pointing to evidence that suggests a reasonable  Schedule 1  Consumer data right" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person must not engage in conduct that misleads or deceives, or is likely to mislead or deceive, another person (the second person) into believing that:  (a) a person is a CDR consumer for CDR data; or  (b) a person is making a valid request or consent, or has satisfied other criteria, for the disclosure of CDR data under the consumer data rules. Note 1: The person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) could be the first-mentioned person, the second person or a third person. Note 2: For enforcement, see Part VI (including section 76 for an order for payment of a pecuniary penalty). Defence  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the conduct is not misleading or deceptive in a material particular.  (3) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (2) bears the burden of adducing or pointing to evidence that suggests a reasonable  Schedule 1  Consumer data right"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "10781f3976cca35c021cbaebd32da6bdcb185f07c8c6a9b1a05dd9086de2d83c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "37"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bo-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bo-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bo-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf> ;
    dc:source "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.37" .
doc:sch-1-sec-56bo a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "56BO Misleading or deceptive conduct—civil penalty" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person must not engage in conduct that misleads or deceives, or is likely to mislead or deceive, another person (the second person) into believing that:  (a) a person is a CDR consumer for CDR data; or  (b) a person is making a valid request or consent, or has satisfied other criteria, for the disclosure of CDR data under the consumer data rules. Note 1: The person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) could be the first-mentioned person, the second person or a third person. Note 2: For enforcement, see Part VI (including section 76 for an order for payment of a pecuniary penalty). Defence  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the conduct is not misleading or deceptive in a material particular.  (3) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (2) bears the burden of adducing or pointing to evidence that suggests a reasonable  Schedule 1  Consumer data right" ;
    cof:pageNumber "37"^^xsd:integer .

