doc:sch-1-sec-56br a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "56BR Ministerial consent to rules required" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The Commission must not make consumer data rules under subsection 56BA(1) unless the Minister has consented, in writing, to the making of the rules. Note: In an emergency, consent is not required (see section 56BS).  Consumer data right  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 63, 2019 Treasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019" ;
    cof:pageNumber "38"^^xsd:integer .

concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bs a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56BS Emergency rules: usual consultation and consent not required"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56bs ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commission may make consumer data rules under subsection 56BA(1):  (a) after consulting the Information Commissioner, but without otherwise complying with section 56BQ; and  (b) without the consent of the Minister as required by section 56BR; if the Commission believes (whether or not that belief is reasonable) that it is necessary to do so in order to avoid a risk of serious harm to:  (c) the efficiency, integrity or stability of any aspect of the Australian economy; or  (d) the interests of consumers. Note: The Commission still needs to comply with section 56BP.  (2) However, a failure to comply with paragraph (1)(a) does not invalidate rules made as described in subsection (1). Note: Such rules may have a limited life (see subsection 56BT(3))." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Commission may make consumer data rules under subsection 56BA(1):  (a) after consulting the Information Commissioner, but without otherwise complying with section 56BQ; and  (b) without the consent of the Minister as required by section 56BR; if the Commission believes (whether or not that belief is reasonable) that it is necessary to do so in order to avoid a risk of serious harm to:  (c) the efficiency, integrity or stability of any aspect of the Australian economy; or  (d) the interests of consumers. Note: The Commission still needs to comply with section 56BP.  (2) However, a failure to comply with paragraph (1)(a) does not invalidate rules made as described in subsection (1). Note: Such rules may have a limited life (see subsection 56BT(3))."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "cff3c5396a0cfd6aa670e6742397c7ddc80442f11c83efbb9387063b27c1b536" ;
    cof:pageNumber "39"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bs-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bs-ss-2 ;
