concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bu a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56BU Charging a fee in inappropriate circumstances when required"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56bu ;
    values:originalText "to disclose CDR data  (1) A person contravenes this subsection if:  (a) the person is a CDR participant for CDR data; and  (b) the person is required under the consumer data rules to disclose all or part of the CDR data; and  (c) the person charges (or causes to be charged) a fee for either or both of the following matters:  (i) the disclosure (or a related disclosure by a designated gateway or other CDR participant for the CDR data);  (ii) the use of the CDR data as the result of the disclosure (or of that related disclosure); and  (d) subsection (2) or any of the following subparagraphs applies:  (i) the CDR data is fee-free CDR data;  (ii) to the extent that the fee is charged for the disclosure of chargeable CDR data—the fee purports to cover a disclosure in circumstances that are not chargeable circumstances;  (iii) to the extent that the fee is charged for the use of chargeable CDR data—the fee purports to cover use in circumstances that are not chargeable circumstances. Note: For enforcement, see Part VI (including section 76 for an order for payment of a pecuniary penalty).  Consumer data right  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 63, 2019 Treasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019  (2) This subsection applies if:  (a) any fee (the reasonable fee):  (i) that has been determined under subsection 56BV(1) for the person; or  (ii) that can be worked out from a method determined under subsection 56BV(1) for the person;  covers either or both of the matters in paragraph (1)(c) of this section; and  (b) the portion of the fee charged as described in that paragraph for those matters exceeds the corresponding portion of the reasonable fee." ;
    skos:definition "to disclose CDR data  (1) A person contravenes this subsection if:  (a) the person is a CDR participant for CDR data; and  (b) the person is required under the consumer data rules to disclose all or part of the CDR data; and  (c) the person charges (or causes to be charged) a fee for either or both of the following matters:  (i) the disclosure (or a related disclosure by a designated gateway or other CDR participant for the CDR data);  (ii) the use of the CDR data as the result of the disclosure (or of that related disclosure); and  (d) subsection (2) or any of the following subparagraphs applies:  (i) the CDR data is fee-free CDR data;  (ii) to the extent that the fee is charged for the disclosure of chargeable CDR data—the fee purports to cover a disclosure in circumstances that are not chargeable circumstances;  (iii) to the extent that the fee is charged for the use of chargeable CDR data—the fee purports to cover use in circumstances that are not chargeable circumstances. Note: For enforcement, see Part VI (including section 76 for an order for payment of a pecuniary penalty).  Consumer data right  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 63, 2019 Treasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019  (2) This subsection applies if:  (a) any fee (the reasonable fee):  (i) that has been determined under subsection 56BV(1) for the person; or  (ii) that can be worked out from a method determined under subsection 56BV(1) for the person;  covers either or both of the matters in paragraph (1)(c) of this section; and  (b) the portion of the fee charged as described in that paragraph for those matters exceeds the corresponding portion of the reasonable fee."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ab419250bfbcebe57f519d1f2d2a07e41d75b1b3017cbc199baf29ef589c2007" ;
    cof:pageNumber "40"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bu-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bu-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf> ;
    dc:source "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.40" .
doc:sch-1-sec-56bu a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "56BU Charging a fee in inappropriate circumstances when required" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "to disclose CDR data  (1) A person contravenes this subsection if:  (a) the person is a CDR participant for CDR data; and  (b) the person is required under the consumer data rules to disclose all or part of the CDR data; and  (c) the person charges (or causes to be charged) a fee for either or both of the following matters:  (i) the disclosure (or a related disclosure by a designated gateway or other CDR participant for the CDR data);  (ii) the use of the CDR data as the result of the disclosure (or of that related disclosure); and  (d) subsection (2) or any of the following subparagraphs applies:  (i) the CDR data is fee-free CDR data;  (ii) to the extent that the fee is charged for the disclosure of chargeable CDR data—the fee purports to cover a disclosure in circumstances that are not chargeable circumstances;  (iii) to the extent that the fee is charged for the use of chargeable CDR data—the fee purports to cover use in circumstances that are not chargeable circumstances. Note: For enforcement, see Part VI (including section 76 for an order for payment of a pecuniary penalty).  Consumer data right  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 63, 2019 Treasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019  (2) This subsection applies if:  (a) any fee (the reasonable fee):  (i) that has been determined under subsection 56BV(1) for the person; or  (ii) that can be worked out from a method determined under subsection 56BV(1) for the person;  covers either or both of the matters in paragraph (1)(c) of this section; and  (b) the portion of the fee charged as described in that paragraph for those matters exceeds the corresponding portion of the reasonable fee." ;
    cof:pageNumber "40"^^xsd:integer .

