doc:sch-1-sec-56bw-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "56BW(3) Review by the Tribunal of determinations specifying" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) If the Tribunal receives an application under this section for a review of a determination, the Tribunal must review the determination.  Consumer data right  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 63, 2019 Treasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019" ;
    cof:pageNumber "42"^^xsd:integer .

concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bx a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56BX Functions and powers of Tribunal"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56bx ;
    values:originalText "(1) On a review of a determination made under subsection 56BV(1), the Tribunal:  (a) may make a decision affirming, setting aside or varying the determination; and  (b) for the purposes of the review, may perform all the functions and exercise all the powers of the Commission.  (2) A decision by the Tribunal affirming, setting aside or varying such a determination is taken for the purposes of this Act (other than sections 56BW to 56BY)) to be a determination of the Commission.  (3) For the purposes of a review by the Tribunal, the member of the Tribunal presiding at the review may require the Commission to give such information, make such reports and provide such other assistance to the Tribunal as the member specifies.  (4) For the purposes of a review, the Tribunal may have regard to any information given, documents produced or evidence given to the Commission in connection with the making of the determination to which the review relates. Note: Division 2 of Part IX applies to proceedings before the Tribunal." ;
    skos:definition "(1) On a review of a determination made under subsection 56BV(1), the Tribunal:  (a) may make a decision affirming, setting aside or varying the determination; and  (b) for the purposes of the review, may perform all the functions and exercise all the powers of the Commission.  (2) A decision by the Tribunal affirming, setting aside or varying such a determination is taken for the purposes of this Act (other than sections 56BW to 56BY)) to be a determination of the Commission.  (3) For the purposes of a review by the Tribunal, the member of the Tribunal presiding at the review may require the Commission to give such information, make such reports and provide such other assistance to the Tribunal as the member specifies.  (4) For the purposes of a review, the Tribunal may have regard to any information given, documents produced or evidence given to the Commission in connection with the making of the determination to which the review relates. Note: Division 2 of Part IX applies to proceedings before the Tribunal."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "881e632501678d6f11066905409604bd72ee2c9a9cf0b989b7180b6d751be9cc" ;
    cof:pageNumber "43"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bx-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56bx-ss-2 ;
