concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ch a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56CH Functions, powers and annual report"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56ch ;
    values:originalText "(1) The functions of the Data Recipient Accreditor are:  (a) to accredit persons under subsection 56CA(1); and  (b) such other functions as are conferred by the consumer data rules.  Consumer data right  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 63, 2019 Treasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019  (2) The Data Recipient Accreditor has the power to do all other things necessary or convenient to be done for or in connection with the performance of the Data Recipient Accreditor’s functions.  (3) To avoid doubt, for a person who is the Data Recipient Accreditor, both:  (a) the person’s functions and powers in their capacity other than as the Data Recipient Accreditor (their primary capacity); and  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—the functions that may be performed, and the powers that may be exercised, by anyone appointed under a Commonwealth law to act as the person in that primary capacity; are taken to include the functions and powers of the Data Recipient Accreditor while the person is the Data Recipient Accreditor.  (4) If:  (a) a person is the Data Recipient Accreditor at any time during a period; and  (b) an annual report for the period is prepared under section 46 of the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013:  (i) by the person in the person’s primary capacity; or  (ii) about the person in the person’s primary capacity; the annual report must include information about the performance of the Data Recipient Accreditor’s functions, and the exercise of the Data Recipient Accreditor’s powers, at that time." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The functions of the Data Recipient Accreditor are:  (a) to accredit persons under subsection 56CA(1); and  (b) such other functions as are conferred by the consumer data rules.  Consumer data right  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 63, 2019 Treasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019  (2) The Data Recipient Accreditor has the power to do all other things necessary or convenient to be done for or in connection with the performance of the Data Recipient Accreditor’s functions.  (3) To avoid doubt, for a person who is the Data Recipient Accreditor, both:  (a) the person’s functions and powers in their capacity other than as the Data Recipient Accreditor (their primary capacity); and  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—the functions that may be performed, and the powers that may be exercised, by anyone appointed under a Commonwealth law to act as the person in that primary capacity; are taken to include the functions and powers of the Data Recipient Accreditor while the person is the Data Recipient Accreditor.  (4) If:  (a) a person is the Data Recipient Accreditor at any time during a period; and  (b) an annual report for the period is prepared under section 46 of the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013:  (i) by the person in the person’s primary capacity; or  (ii) about the person in the person’s primary capacity; the annual report must include information about the performance of the Data Recipient Accreditor’s functions, and the exercise of the Data Recipient Accreditor’s powers, at that time."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0b323c42aec8dde0a816c8dc5ff86af19a2dcdf4f2fb00b06aac6d13408f9a8b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "46"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ch-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ch-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ch-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ch-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf> ;
    dc:source "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.46" .
