doc:sch-1-sec-56ed-ss-5 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "56ED(5) Privacy safeguard 1—open and transparent management of" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(5) If the CDR entity is an accredited data recipient of any CDR data, the CDR entity’s policy must contain the following information:  (a) the classes of CDR data held by (or on behalf of) the CDR entity as an accredited data recipient, and how such CDR data is held;  (b) the purposes for which the CDR entity may collect, hold, use or disclose such CDR data with the consent of a CDR consumer for the CDR data;  (c) how a CDR consumer for such CDR data may access the CDR data and seek the correction of the CDR data;  (d) how a CDR consumer for such CDR data may complain about a failure of the CDR entity to comply with this Part or the consumer data rules, and how the CDR entity will deal with such a complaint;  (e) whether the CDR entity is likely to disclose such CDR data to accredited persons who are based overseas;  (f) if the CDR entity is likely to disclose such CDR data to accredited persons who are based overseas—the countries in which such persons are likely to be based if it is practicable to specify those countries in the policy;  (g) the circumstances in which the CDR entity may disclose such CDR data to a person who is not an accredited person;  (h) the events about which the CDR entity will notify the CDR consumers of such CDR data;  (i) the circumstances in which the CDR entity must delete or de-identify such CDR data in accordance with a request given by a CDR consumer for the CDR data under the consumer data rules." ;
    cof:pageNumber "54"^^xsd:integer .

concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ed-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56ED(6) Privacy safeguard 1—open and transparent management of"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56ed-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) If the CDR entity is a designated gateway for any CDR data, the CDR entity’s policy must contain the following information:  (a) an explanation of how the CDR entity, as a designated gateway, will act between persons to facilitate:  (i) the disclosure of CDR data; or  (ii) the accuracy of CDR data; or  Schedule 1  Consumer data right" ;
    skos:definition "(6) If the CDR entity is a designated gateway for any CDR data, the CDR entity’s policy must contain the following information:  (a) an explanation of how the CDR entity, as a designated gateway, will act between persons to facilitate:  (i) the disclosure of CDR data; or  (ii) the accuracy of CDR data; or  Schedule 1  Consumer data right"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3ad797610cd6e9e2ff6b120a08c5f555ceceeea4f9faef11ab85c33ababad817" ;
    values:partOf concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ed ;
    cof:pageNumber "54"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Civil penalty provision CDR entity must provide information about disclosure and accuracy of CDR data" ;
    dc:description "Yes" ;
