concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ee a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56EE Privacy safeguard 2—anonymity and pseudonymity"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56ee ;
    values:originalText "(1) An accredited data recipient of CDR data must give each CDR consumer for the CDR data the option of using a pseudonym, or not identifying themselves, when dealing with the accredited data recipient in relation to the CDR data. Note: The CDR participant from whom the accredited data recipient acquired the CDR data may be subject to a similar obligation under Australian Privacy Principle 2.  (2) That option may be given to a CDR consumer for the CDR data through a designated gateway for the CDR data.  (3) Subsection (1) does not apply in the circumstances specified in the consumer data rules.  Consumer data right  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 63, 2019 Treasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019  Subdivision C—Collecting CDR data" ;
    skos:definition "(1) An accredited data recipient of CDR data must give each CDR consumer for the CDR data the option of using a pseudonym, or not identifying themselves, when dealing with the accredited data recipient in relation to the CDR data. Note: The CDR participant from whom the accredited data recipient acquired the CDR data may be subject to a similar obligation under Australian Privacy Principle 2.  (2) That option may be given to a CDR consumer for the CDR data through a designated gateway for the CDR data.  (3) Subsection (1) does not apply in the circumstances specified in the consumer data rules.  Consumer data right  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 63, 2019 Treasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019  Subdivision C—Collecting CDR data"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3d76cb491e7362eb97343f612aaca0006393d199454059f8e8b4edb022ddc36b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "56"^^xsd:integer ;
