concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ef a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56EF Privacy safeguard 3—soliciting CDR data from CDR"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56ef ;
    values:originalText "participants  (1) An accredited person must not seek to collect CDR data under the consumer data rules from a CDR participant for the CDR data unless:  (a) a CDR consumer for the CDR data has requested this by giving a valid request under the consumer data rules; and  (b) the person complies with all other requirements in the consumer data rules for the collection of the CDR data from the CDR participant. Note: This subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).  (2) Subsection (1) applies whether the collection is directly from the CDR participant or indirectly from the CDR participant through a designated gateway for the CDR data. Note: The valid request referred to in paragraph (1)(a) could be given through a designated gateway (see section 56BG)." ;
    skos:definition "participants  (1) An accredited person must not seek to collect CDR data under the consumer data rules from a CDR participant for the CDR data unless:  (a) a CDR consumer for the CDR data has requested this by giving a valid request under the consumer data rules; and  (b) the person complies with all other requirements in the consumer data rules for the collection of the CDR data from the CDR participant. Note: This subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).  (2) Subsection (1) applies whether the collection is directly from the CDR participant or indirectly from the CDR participant through a designated gateway for the CDR data. Note: The valid request referred to in paragraph (1)(a) could be given through a designated gateway (see section 56BG)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "34ef94a0ea333af91dd061f0a4f5a567f6a924e1bbee5fb4f3a4131192e4261a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "57"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ef-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ef-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf> ;
    dc:source "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.57" .
doc:sch-1-sec-56ef a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "56EF Privacy safeguard 3—soliciting CDR data from CDR" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "participants  (1) An accredited person must not seek to collect CDR data under the consumer data rules from a CDR participant for the CDR data unless:  (a) a CDR consumer for the CDR data has requested this by giving a valid request under the consumer data rules; and  (b) the person complies with all other requirements in the consumer data rules for the collection of the CDR data from the CDR participant. Note: This subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).  (2) Subsection (1) applies whether the collection is directly from the CDR participant or indirectly from the CDR participant through a designated gateway for the CDR data. Note: The valid request referred to in paragraph (1)(a) could be given through a designated gateway (see section 56BG)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "57"^^xsd:integer .

