    prov:wasDerivedFrom <treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf> ;
    dc:source "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.57" .
doc:sch-1-sec-56eg a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "56EG Privacy safeguard 4—dealing with unsolicited CDR data from" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "CDR participants  (1) If a person:  (a) while the person is an accredited person, collects CDR data from a CDR participant for the CDR data:  (i) purportedly under the consumer data rules; but  (ii) not as the result of seeking to collect that CDR data under the consumer data rules; and  (b) is not required to retain that CDR data by or under an Australian law or a court/tribunal order; the person must destroy that CDR data as soon as practicable. Note: This subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).  (2) Subsection (1) applies whether the collection is directly from the CDR participant or indirectly from the CDR participant through a designated gateway for the CDR data.  Schedule 1  Consumer data right" ;
    cof:pageNumber "57"^^xsd:integer .

concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56eg-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56EG(1) Privacy safeguard 4—dealing with unsolicited CDR data from"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56eg-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If a person:  (a) while the person is an accredited person, collects CDR data from a CDR participant for the CDR data:  (i) purportedly under the consumer data rules; but  (ii) not as the result of seeking to collect that CDR data under the consumer data rules; and  (b) is not required to retain that CDR data by or under an Australian law or a court/tribunal order; the person must destroy that CDR data as soon as practicable. Note: This subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If a person:  (a) while the person is an accredited person, collects CDR data from a CDR participant for the CDR data:  (i) purportedly under the consumer data rules; but  (ii) not as the result of seeking to collect that CDR data under the consumer data rules; and  (b) is not required to retain that CDR data by or under an Australian law or a court/tribunal order; the person must destroy that CDR data as soon as practicable. Note: This subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU)."@en ;
