    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56en-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) If an accredited data recipient of CDR data is disclosing the CDR data when:  (a) required under the consumer data rules to do so in response to a valid request from a CDR consumer for the CDR data; or  (b) otherwise required, or authorised, under the consumer data rules to do so; the accredited data recipient must take reasonable steps to ensure that the CDR data is, having regard to the purpose for which it is held, accurate, up to date and complete. Note 1: This subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).  Schedule 1  Consumer data right" ;
    skos:definition "(2) If an accredited data recipient of CDR data is disclosing the CDR data when:  (a) required under the consumer data rules to do so in response to a valid request from a CDR consumer for the CDR data; or  (b) otherwise required, or authorised, under the consumer data rules to do so; the accredited data recipient must take reasonable steps to ensure that the CDR data is, having regard to the purpose for which it is held, accurate, up to date and complete. Note 1: This subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).  Schedule 1  Consumer data right"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1d125cb352e20acf0be4a8205f1e2b9784dcef3c0fd8b2bcdb73d79e2dcb5ebb" ;
    values:partOf concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56en ;
    cof:pageNumber "63"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Accredited data recipient must ensure CDR data is accurate, up to date and complete." ;
