doc:sch-1-sec-56en-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "56EN(2) Privacy safeguard 11—quality of CDR data" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) If an accredited data recipient of CDR data is disclosing the CDR data when:  (a) required under the consumer data rules to do so in response to a valid request from a CDR consumer for the CDR data; or  (b) otherwise required, or authorised, under the consumer data rules to do so; the accredited data recipient must take reasonable steps to ensure that the CDR data is, having regard to the purpose for which it is held, accurate, up to date and complete. Note 1: This subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).  Schedule 1  Consumer data right" ;
    cof:pageNumber "63"^^xsd:integer .

concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56eo a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56EO Privacy safeguard 12—security of CDR data, and destruction"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56eo ;
    values:originalText "or de-identification of redundant CDR data  (1) Each person (a CDR entity) who is:  (a) an accredited data recipient of CDR data; or  (b) a designated gateway for CDR data;  Consumer data right  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 63, 2019 Treasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019  must take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to protect the CDR data from:  (c) misuse, interference and loss; and  (d) unauthorised access, modification or disclosure. Note: This subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).  (2) If:  (a) the CDR entity no longer needs any of that CDR data for either of the following purposes (the redundant data):  (i) a purpose permitted under the consumer data rules;  (ii) a purpose for which the person is able to use or disclose it in accordance with this Division; and  (b) the CDR entity is not required to retain the redundant data by or under an Australian law or a court/tribunal order; and  (c) the redundant data does not relate to any current or anticipated:  (i) legal proceedings; or  (ii) dispute resolution proceedings;  to which the CDR entity is a party; the CDR entity must take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to destroy the redundant data or to ensure that the redundant data is de-identified. Note 1: This subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU). Note 2: Australian Privacy Principle 11 will not apply for paragraph (b) (see paragraph 56EC(4)(a) or (d)). Subdivision F—Correction of CDR data" ;
    skos:definition "or de-identification of redundant CDR data  (1) Each person (a CDR entity) who is:  (a) an accredited data recipient of CDR data; or  (b) a designated gateway for CDR data;  Consumer data right  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 63, 2019 Treasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019  must take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to protect the CDR data from:  (c) misuse, interference and loss; and  (d) unauthorised access, modification or disclosure. Note: This subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).  (2) If:  (a) the CDR entity no longer needs any of that CDR data for either of the following purposes (the redundant data):  (i) a purpose permitted under the consumer data rules;  (ii) a purpose for which the person is able to use or disclose it in accordance with this Division; and  (b) the CDR entity is not required to retain the redundant data by or under an Australian law or a court/tribunal order; and  (c) the redundant data does not relate to any current or anticipated:  (i) legal proceedings; or  (ii) dispute resolution proceedings;  to which the CDR entity is a party; the CDR entity must take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to destroy the redundant data or to ensure that the redundant data is de-identified. Note 1: This subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU). Note 2: Australian Privacy Principle 11 will not apply for paragraph (b) (see paragraph 56EC(4)(a) or (d)). Subdivision F—Correction of CDR data"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "28b144543f070068c9f57dea356d8df7aa38daf6b056a2732506024e00ee6537" ;
    cof:pageNumber "64"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56eo-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56eo-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf> ;
    dc:source "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.64" .
doc:sch-1-sec-56eo a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "56EO Privacy safeguard 12—security of CDR data, and destruction" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "or de-identification of redundant CDR data  (1) Each person (a CDR entity) who is:  (a) an accredited data recipient of CDR data; or  (b) a designated gateway for CDR data;  Consumer data right  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 63, 2019 Treasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019  must take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to protect the CDR data from:  (c) misuse, interference and loss; and  (d) unauthorised access, modification or disclosure. Note: This subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU).  (2) If:  (a) the CDR entity no longer needs any of that CDR data for either of the following purposes (the redundant data):  (i) a purpose permitted under the consumer data rules;  (ii) a purpose for which the person is able to use or disclose it in accordance with this Division; and  (b) the CDR entity is not required to retain the redundant data by or under an Australian law or a court/tribunal order; and  (c) the redundant data does not relate to any current or anticipated:  (i) legal proceedings; or  (ii) dispute resolution proceedings;  to which the CDR entity is a party; the CDR entity must take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to destroy the redundant data or to ensure that the redundant data is de-identified. Note 1: This subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU). Note 2: Australian Privacy Principle 11 will not apply for paragraph (b) (see paragraph 56EC(4)(a) or (d)). Subdivision F—Correction of CDR data" ;
    cof:pageNumber "64"^^xsd:integer .

