doc:sch-1-sec-56eo-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "56EO(1) Privacy safeguard 12—security of CDR data, and destruction" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Each person (a CDR entity) who is:  (a) an accredited data recipient of CDR data; or  (b) a designated gateway for CDR data;  Consumer data right  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 63, 2019 Treasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019  must take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to protect the CDR data from:  (c) misuse, interference and loss; and  (d) unauthorised access, modification or disclosure. Note: This subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "64"^^xsd:integer .

concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56eo-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56EO(2) Privacy safeguard 12—security of CDR data, and destruction"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56eo-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) If:  (a) the CDR entity no longer needs any of that CDR data for either of the following purposes (the redundant data):  (i) a purpose permitted under the consumer data rules;  (ii) a purpose for which the person is able to use or disclose it in accordance with this Division; and  (b) the CDR entity is not required to retain the redundant data by or under an Australian law or a court/tribunal order; and  (c) the redundant data does not relate to any current or anticipated:  (i) legal proceedings; or  (ii) dispute resolution proceedings;  to which the CDR entity is a party; the CDR entity must take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to destroy the redundant data or to ensure that the redundant data is de-identified. Note 1: This subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU). Note 2: Australian Privacy Principle 11 will not apply for paragraph (b) (see paragraph 56EC(4)(a) or (d)). Subdivision F—Correction of CDR data" ;
    skos:definition "(2) If:  (a) the CDR entity no longer needs any of that CDR data for either of the following purposes (the redundant data):  (i) a purpose permitted under the consumer data rules;  (ii) a purpose for which the person is able to use or disclose it in accordance with this Division; and  (b) the CDR entity is not required to retain the redundant data by or under an Australian law or a court/tribunal order; and  (c) the redundant data does not relate to any current or anticipated:  (i) legal proceedings; or  (ii) dispute resolution proceedings;  to which the CDR entity is a party; the CDR entity must take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to destroy the redundant data or to ensure that the redundant data is de-identified. Note 1: This subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU). Note 2: Australian Privacy Principle 11 will not apply for paragraph (b) (see paragraph 56EC(4)(a) or (d)). Subdivision F—Correction of CDR data"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7adda229a1544bc6d1e8065b2aaceadb598c1ef1c0b68145fb454bc1ab4e640b" ;
    values:partOf concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56eo ;
    cof:pageNumber "64"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Destroy redundant CDR data if no longer needed for permitted purposes and not required by law or court order." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
