doc:sch-1-sec-56eo-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "56EO(2) Privacy safeguard 12—security of CDR data, and destruction" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) If:  (a) the CDR entity no longer needs any of that CDR data for either of the following purposes (the redundant data):  (i) a purpose permitted under the consumer data rules;  (ii) a purpose for which the person is able to use or disclose it in accordance with this Division; and  (b) the CDR entity is not required to retain the redundant data by or under an Australian law or a court/tribunal order; and  (c) the redundant data does not relate to any current or anticipated:  (i) legal proceedings; or  (ii) dispute resolution proceedings;  to which the CDR entity is a party; the CDR entity must take the steps specified in the consumer data rules to destroy the redundant data or to ensure that the redundant data is de-identified. Note 1: This subsection is a civil penalty provision (see section 56EU). Note 2: Australian Privacy Principle 11 will not apply for paragraph (b) (see paragraph 56EC(4)(a) or (d)). Subdivision F—Correction of CDR data" ;
    cof:pageNumber "64"^^xsd:integer .

concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ep a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56EP Privacy safeguard 13—correction of CDR data"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56ep ;
    values:originalText "Obligation on data holders  (1) If:  (a) a CDR consumer for CDR data gives a request to a data holder of the CDR data (including a request given through a designated gateway for the CDR data); and  (b) the request is for the data holder to correct the CDR data; and  (c) the data holder was earlier required or authorised under the consumer data rules to disclose the CDR data;  Schedule 1  Consumer data right" ;
    skos:definition "Obligation on data holders  (1) If:  (a) a CDR consumer for CDR data gives a request to a data holder of the CDR data (including a request given through a designated gateway for the CDR data); and  (b) the request is for the data holder to correct the CDR data; and  (c) the data holder was earlier required or authorised under the consumer data rules to disclose the CDR data;  Schedule 1  Consumer data right"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e7c7bbc40371f7a4334d9bcf306841af328fefe8d7053d858a7a758d9a7bdc22" ;
    cof:pageNumber "65"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Data holder must correct CDR data upon request from consumer." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf> ;
    dc:source "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.65" ;
    cml:asserts concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ep-norm .
