concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56eu-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56EU(4) Civil penalty provisions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56eu-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) For the purposes of Part 4 of the Regulatory Powers Act, each of the following courts is a relevant court in relation to each privacy safeguard penalty provision:  (a) the Federal Court;  (b) the Federal Circuit Court;  (c) a court of a State or Territory that has jurisdiction in relation to the matter. Act or omission also contravening a civil penalty provision of the consumer data rules" ;
    skos:definition "(4) For the purposes of Part 4 of the Regulatory Powers Act, each of the following courts is a relevant court in relation to each privacy safeguard penalty provision:  (a) the Federal Court;  (b) the Federal Circuit Court;  (c) a court of a State or Territory that has jurisdiction in relation to the matter. Act or omission also contravening a civil penalty provision of the consumer data rules"@en ;
