concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ey-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56EY(5) Actions for damages"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56ey-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) The following are conferred with jurisdiction to hear and determine actions under subsection (1):  (a) the Federal Circuit Court;  (b) subject to the Constitution, the several courts of the Territories. This subsection does not enable an inferior court of a Territory to grant a remedy of a kind that the court is unable to grant under the law of that Territory. Note: State courts and the Federal Court also have jurisdiction for these actions (see subsection 39(2) and paragraph 39B(1A)(c) of the Judiciary Act 1903)." ;
    skos:definition "(5) The following are conferred with jurisdiction to hear and determine actions under subsection (1):  (a) the Federal Circuit Court;  (b) subject to the Constitution, the several courts of the Territories. This subsection does not enable an inferior court of a Territory to grant a remedy of a kind that the court is unable to grant under the law of that Territory. Note: State courts and the Federal Court also have jurisdiction for these actions (see subsection 39(2) and paragraph 39B(1A)(c) of the Judiciary Act 1903)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b038aa3635ef872cf80721ba8da616204611cbc888c7817aa49fd5a81769e785" ;
    values:partOf concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ey ;
    cof:pageNumber "76"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Jurisdiction for actions under subsection (1)" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
