concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56fd a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56FD Legal effect of data standards"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56fd ;
    values:originalText "(1) A contract is taken to be in force between:  (a) a data holder of CDR data to which a binding data standard applies; and  (b) each accredited person;  Consumer data right  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 63, 2019 Treasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019  under which each of those persons:  (c) agrees to observe the standard to the extent that the standard applies to the person; and  (d) agrees to engage in conduct that the person is required by the standard to engage in. Note: This means the data holder will be taken to have a separate contract with each accredited person.  (2) If there is a designated gateway for CDR data to which a binding data standard applies, a contract is taken to be in force between:  (a) a data holder of the CDR data; and  (b) the designated gateway for the CDR data; and  (c) each accredited person; under which each of those persons:  (d) agrees to observe the standard to the extent that the standard applies to the person; and  (e) agrees to engage in conduct that the person is required by the standard to engage in. Note: This means the data holder will be taken to have a separate 3-party contract with the designated gateway and each accredited person.  (3) However, if there is an inconsistency between a data standard, and the consumer data rules, those rules prevail over the standard to the extent of the inconsistency." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A contract is taken to be in force between:  (a) a data holder of CDR data to which a binding data standard applies; and  (b) each accredited person;  Consumer data right  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 63, 2019 Treasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019  under which each of those persons:  (c) agrees to observe the standard to the extent that the standard applies to the person; and  (d) agrees to engage in conduct that the person is required by the standard to engage in. Note: This means the data holder will be taken to have a separate contract with each accredited person.  (2) If there is a designated gateway for CDR data to which a binding data standard applies, a contract is taken to be in force between:  (a) a data holder of the CDR data; and  (b) the designated gateway for the CDR data; and  (c) each accredited person; under which each of those persons:  (d) agrees to observe the standard to the extent that the standard applies to the person; and  (e) agrees to engage in conduct that the person is required by the standard to engage in. Note: This means the data holder will be taken to have a separate 3-party contract with the designated gateway and each accredited person.  (3) However, if there is an inconsistency between a data standard, and the consumer data rules, those rules prevail over the standard to the extent of the inconsistency."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ee7d6bb9bd38b15c51ffb5b1bd930485a0e8bd11e4422611b98b51438f7b7ba9" ;
    cof:pageNumber "80"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56fd-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56fd-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56fd-ss-3 ;
