doc:sch-1-sec-56fd-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "56FD(2) Legal effect of data standards" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) If there is a designated gateway for CDR data to which a binding data standard applies, a contract is taken to be in force between:  (a) a data holder of the CDR data; and  (b) the designated gateway for the CDR data; and  (c) each accredited person; under which each of those persons:  (d) agrees to observe the standard to the extent that the standard applies to the person; and  (e) agrees to engage in conduct that the person is required by the standard to engage in. Note: This means the data holder will be taken to have a separate 3-party contract with the designated gateway and each accredited person." ;
    cof:pageNumber "80"^^xsd:integer .

concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56fd-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56FD(3) Legal effect of data standards"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56fd-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) However, if there is an inconsistency between a data standard, and the consumer data rules, those rules prevail over the standard to the extent of the inconsistency." ;
    skos:definition "(3) However, if there is an inconsistency between a data standard, and the consumer data rules, those rules prevail over the standard to the extent of the inconsistency."@en ;
