concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56fe a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56FE Enforcement of binding data standards"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56fe ;
    values:originalText "(1) If a person who is under an obligation to comply with a binding data standard fails to meet that obligation, an application to the Court may be made by:  (a) the Commission; or  (b) a person aggrieved by the failure.  (2) After giving an opportunity to be heard to the applicant and the person against whom the order is sought, the Court may make an order giving directions to:  (a) the person against whom the order is sought; or  (b) if that person is a body corporate—the directors of the body corporate;  Schedule 1  Consumer data right" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If a person who is under an obligation to comply with a binding data standard fails to meet that obligation, an application to the Court may be made by:  (a) the Commission; or  (b) a person aggrieved by the failure.  (2) After giving an opportunity to be heard to the applicant and the person against whom the order is sought, the Court may make an order giving directions to:  (a) the person against whom the order is sought; or  (b) if that person is a body corporate—the directors of the body corporate;  Schedule 1  Consumer data right"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4506af6af836fe7f083adcc899c5824c67aad94dba7c6d62f0c667eb30a585e3" ;
    cof:pageNumber "81"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56fe-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56fe-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf> ;
    dc:source "treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019.pdf, p.81" .
