concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56fg a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56FG Appointment of the Data Standards Chair"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56fg ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Data Standards Chair is to be appointed, on a full-time basis or a part-time basis, by the Minister by written instrument.  (2) The Data Standards Chair holds office for the period specified in the instrument of appointment. The period must not exceed 3 years. Note 1: The Minister will be the Data Standards Chair in the absence of an appointment under this section (see the definition of Data Standards Chair in subsection 4(1)). Note 2: The Data Standards Chair may be reappointed (see section 33AA of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Data Standards Chair is to be appointed, on a full-time basis or a part-time basis, by the Minister by written instrument.  (2) The Data Standards Chair holds office for the period specified in the instrument of appointment. The period must not exceed 3 years. Note 1: The Minister will be the Data Standards Chair in the absence of an appointment under this section (see the definition of Data Standards Chair in subsection 4(1)). Note 2: The Data Standards Chair may be reappointed (see section 33AA of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1ac7f24902c79391f0c0e6027d47dbcd1296e475c589104639b1b03bdca76571" ;
