concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56gc a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56GC Complying with requirements to provide CDR data:"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56gc ;
    values:originalText "protection from liability  (1) If:  (a) a CDR participant, or designated gateway, for CDR data (the CDR entity):  (i) provides the CDR data to another person; or  Consumer data right  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 63, 2019 Treasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019  (ii) otherwise allows another person access to the CDR data; and  (b) the CDR entity does so, in good faith, in compliance with:  (i) this Part; and  (ii) regulations made for the purposes of this Part; and  (iii) the consumer data rules; the CDR entity is not liable to an action or other proceeding, whether civil or criminal, for or in relation to the matter in paragraph (a). Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in subsection (1) for a criminal action or criminal proceeding (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).  (2) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (1) in relation to a civil action or civil proceeding bears an evidential burden in relation to that matter.  (3) In this section: evidential burden, in relation to a matter, means the burden of adducing or pointing to evidence that suggests a reasonable possibility that the matter exists or does not exist." ;
    skos:definition "protection from liability  (1) If:  (a) a CDR participant, or designated gateway, for CDR data (the CDR entity):  (i) provides the CDR data to another person; or  Consumer data right  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 63, 2019 Treasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019  (ii) otherwise allows another person access to the CDR data; and  (b) the CDR entity does so, in good faith, in compliance with:  (i) this Part; and  (ii) regulations made for the purposes of this Part; and  (iii) the consumer data rules; the CDR entity is not liable to an action or other proceeding, whether civil or criminal, for or in relation to the matter in paragraph (a). Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in subsection (1) for a criminal action or criminal proceeding (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).  (2) A person who wishes to rely on subsection (1) in relation to a civil action or civil proceeding bears an evidential burden in relation to that matter.  (3) In this section: evidential burden, in relation to a matter, means the burden of adducing or pointing to evidence that suggests a reasonable possibility that the matter exists or does not exist."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e4c77fb00eb1d26520455bd296ab7e8cd6f38df25429451d65932978aabca6b1" ;
    cof:pageNumber "88"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56gc-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56gc-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56gc-ss-3 ;
