concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ge a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56GE Exemptions and modifications by regulations"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-56ge ;
    values:originalText "(1) The provisions covered by this section are:  (a) the following provisions:  (i) the provisions of this Part;  (ii) the provisions of regulations made for the purposes of the provisions of this Part;  (iii) the provisions of the consumer data rules; and  (b) definitions in this Act, or in the regulations or consumer data rules, as they apply to references in provisions referred to in paragraph (a).  (2) The regulations may:  (a) exempt a particular person, in relation to particular CDR data or one or more classes of CDR data, from all or specified provisions covered by this section; or  (b) exempt a class of persons, in relation to particular CDR data or one or more classes of CDR data, from all or specified provisions covered by this section; or  (c) declare that provisions covered by this section apply in relation to:  (i) a particular person in relation to particular CDR data or one or more classes of CDR data; or  (ii) a class of persons in relation to particular CDR data or one or more classes of CDR data;  as if specified provisions were omitted, modified or varied as specified in the declaration.  (3) An exemption under paragraph (2)(a) or (b), or a declaration under paragraph (2)(c):  (a) may or may not be limited to a specified period; and  Consumer data right  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 63, 2019 Treasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019  (b) may apply unconditionally or subject to specified conditions." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The provisions covered by this section are:  (a) the following provisions:  (i) the provisions of this Part;  (ii) the provisions of regulations made for the purposes of the provisions of this Part;  (iii) the provisions of the consumer data rules; and  (b) definitions in this Act, or in the regulations or consumer data rules, as they apply to references in provisions referred to in paragraph (a).  (2) The regulations may:  (a) exempt a particular person, in relation to particular CDR data or one or more classes of CDR data, from all or specified provisions covered by this section; or  (b) exempt a class of persons, in relation to particular CDR data or one or more classes of CDR data, from all or specified provisions covered by this section; or  (c) declare that provisions covered by this section apply in relation to:  (i) a particular person in relation to particular CDR data or one or more classes of CDR data; or  (ii) a class of persons in relation to particular CDR data or one or more classes of CDR data;  as if specified provisions were omitted, modified or varied as specified in the declaration.  (3) An exemption under paragraph (2)(a) or (b), or a declaration under paragraph (2)(c):  (a) may or may not be limited to a specified period; and  Consumer data right  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 63, 2019 Treasury Laws Amendment (Consumer Data Right) Act 2019  (b) may apply unconditionally or subject to specified conditions."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "92ed6a9017d9dd6c1e33087e4371c21378b8a09a9a8771367a9be9685ea5685e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "90"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ge-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ge-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:treasury-laws-amendment-consumer-data-right-act-2019-sch-1-sec-56ge-ss-3 ;
